<title>USA: US Treasury, Wal-Mart hold talks on Cuban pajamas.</title>
<headline>US Treasury, Wal-Mart hold talks on Cuban pajamas.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lawyers for retailing giant Wal-Mart Stores Inc. are talking with the U.S. Treasury Department about a cross-border tug-of-war over whether Wal-Mart may sell Cuban-made pajamas in Canada, a Treasury official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Canadian government has pressured Wal-Mart Canada into putting the cotton pajamas back on store shelves, putting the retailer in breach of U.S. laws aimed at bringing economic pressure against the Cuban government headed by President Fidel Castro.</p>
</text>
